    "Synthetic, hand-written fixtures only; no real mail, no real people, reserved/synthetic domains.",
    "'file' is relative to tests/fixtures/email_risk. 'config' applies to .eml files (JSON fixtures carry org_context).",
    "label: malicious|benign. A prediction is positive when risk_level >= MEDIUM (HIGH threshold is reported too).",
    "critical: malicious executive/payment attack; predicting LOW/UNKNOWN is a CRITICAL_FALSE_NEGATIVE.",
    "expected_family / acceptable_families: attack-family attribution is scored only on detected malicious cases.",
    "split: core (24 required categories) | adversarial (obfuscation / evasion probes).",
    "requires ['qr_decoder']: skipped (and reported as skipped) when Pillow + zxing-cpp are not installed.",
    "The author of the rules also wrote these fixtures: results measure rule coverage of known patterns, not generalization."
